      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "The Three Points fair opening (bunting, fiddle, tar-and-meat smell, banners crossing ropes, soldiers sharing wine before killing each other) delivers genuine sensory seduction, but this texture is front-loaded in the first few paragraphs and then abandoned for a long stretch of procedural plot machinery \u2014 clerks, ledgers, brackets, boons, manifests \u2014 where GLMZ\u0027s strange-beautiful quality gives way to functional exposition and dialogue-heavy negotiation scenes.",
      "Fix": "Thread more of that lived-in-wrong sensory texture (the graft\u0027s hum under skin, the Sinterkin\u0027s flat unhurried gaze, the construct\u0027s steam-vent rhythms) through the long middle stretch of political and financial maneuvering so allure doesn\u0027t get crowded out by mechanism."
    },
    {
      "Key": "open_grounded",
      "Title": "Open with the world doing its work",
      "Status": "pass",
      "Evidence": "The opening paragraphs establish Three Points as a recurring, ritualized truce-fair through grounded sensory detail (bunting left up since last time, badly-tuned fiddle, tar and roasting meat) and a toll-master who \u0027does not care who you are\u0027 and counts coin \u0027because he has\u0027 done it ten thousand times \u2014 the world functioning on its own logic before Kaeric\u0027s personal crisis (the customs board) intrudes.",
      "Fix": null
